## Context

Child of master ticket 0650. The existing duplicate-work arm proves only that a
second reader joining a settled index does not restart completed work. R13's
honest restatement instead requires unique passage commits and bounds duplicate
compute during failover. This child owns those observables and assertions; it
does not own query survival (0651) or the full soak workload (0653).

## Actions

- Keep and accurately rename/document the settled-company regression.
- Drive overlapping work on one shared data directory and force conductor
  handover at controlled embed-batch and document-work points.
- Observe passage commit identity and fail on a duplicate commit.
- Measure the two categories of duplicate compute against the bound owned by
  `SPEC.md`; do not restate its numbers here.
- Add focused controls for double commit, excess embed work, excess document
  work, and observability that is absent, reset or process-local.

## Test

- [ ] Correct overlapping work and each bounded failover pass.
- [ ] Each one-purpose over-bound or double-commit fixture fails independently.
- [ ] An unfired fault or inadequate observability cannot produce PASS.
- [ ] The settled-company regression remains green and makes no broader claim.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Unique commits and both duplicate-compute categories have distinct checks
      and `falsified_by` descriptions.
- [ ] Every detector has been seen red before green.
- [ ] Targeted unit tests and acceptance fixtures pass.
- [ ] Real-target evidence is committed or the missing target capability is
      reported as a non-pass state.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass.
